root: /home/u
note: the optional harness opencode is skipped: it is not installed (opencode not found on PATH and no /home/u/.config/opencode directory)

claudecode · replace · keeps your login
  binary: /usr/bin/claude
  config: /home/u/.claude
  keeps login: /home/u/.claude/.credentials.json
  keeps history: /home/u/.claude/history.jsonl, /home/u/.claude/projects

antigravity-cli · replace · keeps your login
  binary: /usr/bin/agy
  config: /home/u/.gemini
  keeps state: /home/u/.gemini/config/.migrated
  statusLine runs tool hello: sh /home/u/.dotai/tools/hello.sh

claudecode
  wipe       /home/u/.claude/CLAUDE.md
  wipe       /home/u/.claude/agents
  wipe       /home/u/CLAUDE.md
             warning: other tools that read ~/CLAUDE.md lose it until a restore
  wipe key   /home/u/.claude.json · mcpServers
  wipe key   /home/u/.claude.json · projects["C:/work"].allowedTools
  create     /home/u/.claude/CLAUDE.md

antigravity-cli
  wipe       /home/u/.gemini/GEMINI.md
             warning: Gemini CLI reads it too, and loses it until a restore
  create     /home/u/.gemini/config/GEMINI.md

tools
  create     /home/u/.dotai/tools/hello.sh

refused
  CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is set, so claudecode may read its configuration from somewhere a replace install does not reset: unset it, then install again

